course: dictionary
lesson: 12179
title: Formal words: concur
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to formal writing, the kind used by judges, committees and scientists. Concur is one of them. Its main meaning is to agree: «The other judges concurred» means the other judges all agreed.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Judges make decisions together, so concurred tells you they had the same view. Swap in agreed and check: «The other judges agreed» still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: Concur can also mean to happen at the same time. This meaning is rarer, so the sentence around it gives the clue.
fact: Concur means to agree with someone or with an opinion.
fact: «The other judges concurred» means the other judges agreed.
fact: Concur is a formal word. You will meet it in exam papers, reports and committee notes, more than in chatty talk.
fact: Concur can also mean to happen at the same time, as in «The two events concurred on the same day.»
fact: The forms are concur, concurs, concurred and concurring. You say «I concur with you», with the word with after it.
exercise: «The committee members all concurred with the plan.» What does concurred mean? | *Agreed | Left the room | Forgot | Argued
exercise: «The scientists concurred that the results were correct.» Which word could replace concurred without changing the meaning? | *Agreed | Ignored | Disagreed | Questioned
exercise: «Both events concurred on Friday.» What does concurred mean here? | Were cancelled | *Happened at the same time | Ended early | Asked for help
test: «I concur with your view, so we will vote yes.» What does concur mean? | Shout | Refuse | *Agree | Forget
test: «The two bells rang and concurred at noon.» What does concurred mean here? | Broke | Moved away | Grew quiet | *Happened at the same time
exam: Which sentence uses concur correctly? | I concur the committee's decision. | I concurred up the stairs. | *I concur with the committee's decision. | The bus will concur at the station.
